# AGENTS.md — $HOME

## chezmoi-managed files

Many dotfiles under this home directory are managed by
[chezmoi](https://www.chezmoi.io). The live files are **rendered output** —
editing them directly is lost on the next `chezmoi apply`.

Before editing any file, resolve it to its chezmoi **source** (this falls
back to the path itself when the file is not managed):

```bash
src=$(chezmoi source-path "${file}" 2>/dev/null || printf '%s' "${file}")
```

Edit `${src}`, not `${file}` — that guarantees you always edit the source.
(If `${src}` is a `*.tmpl` or an encrypted source, you're editing chezmoi
template/ciphertext, not the final rendered text.)

After finishing the edit of ANY file, sync it back to `$HOME`. The guard
uses the original target path, so it's a no-op for unmanaged files:

```bash
chezmoi source-path "${file}" >/dev/null 2>&1 && chezmoi apply "${file}"
```
